00:32:47,100 --> 00:32:49,580
He has, like, this big real estate business.

400
00:32:49,580 --> 00:32:54,420
And when Chicago fires happened in, like, 1831, he loses everything that he has.

401
00:32:54,420 --> 00:32:56,020
He loses everything that he has.

402
00:32:56,020 --> 00:33:00,120
There's this kind of, like, at that point, there was, like, this wave of sickness.

403
00:33:00,120 --> 00:33:04,740
He has, like, five kids and loses a four-year-old son to, like, Scarlet View.

404
00:33:04,740 --> 00:33:10,120
And, you know, in the aftermath of that, he starts rebuilding this business.

405
00:33:10,120 --> 00:33:14,900
And a couple years after that, he feels that what his family needs is a vacation.

406
00:33:14,900 --> 00:33:16,960
So, they plan a trip.

407
00:33:16,960 --> 00:33:19,920
And at that point, it was, like, a trip on a ship.

408
00:33:19,920 --> 00:33:23,960
So, like, you have to, like, you know, it takes weeks to get to Europe.

409
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:28,560
So, at the last minute of that trip, he has something come up with his business.

410
00:33:28,560 --> 00:33:29,980
So, he has to stay behind for a few days.

411
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:34,440
So, he sends his wife and his four daughters on the ship, and he stays behind.

412
00:33:34,440 --> 00:33:41,420
That ship hits another ship on the way to Europe, and the ship sinks.

413
00:33:41,420 --> 00:33:44,340
And most everybody dies.

414
00:33:44,340 --> 00:33:50,200
Somehow, his wife is rescued by a boat, but his daughters die.

415
00:33:51,580 --> 00:33:54,680
And when his wife finally makes it to shore, she sends a telegram.

416
00:33:54,680 --> 00:34:01,840
And all the telegram says to her husband, he's saved, alone, what shall I do?

417
00:34:01,840 --> 00:34:09,760
When her husband gets a telegram, he gets on the first boat that he can, and he's on his way to see his wife.

418
00:34:09,760 --> 00:34:15,460
And because this, you know, event had become famous and had caused this commotion,

419
00:34:15,460 --> 00:34:21,320
when they're going towards a certain point on the journey, the captain calls her husband to his quarters.

420
00:34:21,320 --> 00:34:27,700
And he says, hey, just so you know, what we're going through right now on the ship, this is where the crash happened.

421
00:34:27,700 --> 00:34:38,500
And on the aftermath of that, on the ship, on his way to see his wife, that's all he has left.

422
00:34:39,760 --> 00:34:41,060
He writes,

423
00:34:41,060 --> 00:34:47,340
When peace, like a river, attendeth my way.

424
00:34:47,340 --> 00:34:51,920
When sorrows, like sea billows, roll.

425
00:34:51,920 --> 00:35:01,000
Whatever, my Lord, thou hast told me to say, it is well.

426
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:04,560
It is well with my soul.

427
00:35:06,660 --> 00:35:14,740
Probably the most terrible thing that any of us could remind us of happening, happens to him.

428
00:35:14,740 --> 00:35:21,640
And there's something about that in our life with God that he has.

429
00:35:21,640 --> 00:35:25,200
And he's like, I'm in this terrible moment.

430
00:35:25,200 --> 00:35:28,960
And I love the imagery of water, right?

431
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:36,700
Because he's saying, sorrow is hitting my life like the waves of the ocean.

432
00:35:36,700 --> 00:35:40,900
Pain is hitting my life.

433
00:35:40,900 --> 00:35:43,080
Loss.

434
00:35:43,080 --> 00:35:44,660
Grief.

435
00:35:44,660 --> 00:35:46,280
Heartbreak.

436
00:35:46,280 --> 00:35:48,020
Disappointment.

437
00:35:48,020 --> 00:35:49,640
Like, those things don't go away.

438
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:50,560
We live in this world.

439
00:35:50,560 --> 00:35:53,500
Jesus said, I pray that you don't take them out of the world without you.

440
00:35:53,500 --> 00:35:55,040
Keep them in the world, right?

441
00:35:55,240 --> 00:35:57,740
Like, when we're alive, we're in the midst of that.

442
00:35:57,740 --> 00:36:05,480
One thing that I used to in my congregation in BC is like, you know, one of the biggest points of tension in our life is that we don't get to skip our own lives.

443
00:36:07,060 --> 00:36:08,400
And so much of a time, that's what we want.

444
00:36:08,400 --> 00:36:10,860
I will have peace if I can get over it.

445
00:36:10,860 --> 00:36:13,380
I will tell, I've been talking to a pastor in front of mine.

446
00:36:13,380 --> 00:36:15,420
I said, I wish it could be next year.

447
00:36:15,420 --> 00:36:16,160
Right?

448
00:36:16,160 --> 00:36:17,980
And then I know where I'm working.

449
00:36:17,980 --> 00:36:19,420
I know everything, where everything.

450
00:36:19,420 --> 00:36:21,420
And like, it's a daily grind.

451
00:36:21,420 --> 00:36:22,580
I just feel hard.

452
00:36:22,580 --> 00:36:30,160
And I was like, I'm in the middle of this ocean, this storm coming over my last.

453
00:36:30,200 --> 00:36:37,620
And then he said, but somehow in the middle of that, there's a river of peace coming through.

454
00:36:37,620 --> 00:36:48,800
And what Jesus offers us, what Jesus invites us to is that if you give your life over to me, if you dwell with me,

455
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:57,420
if you pray when things are on, if you're thankful for what I have in you, if you meditate in me, if you dwell in me,

456
00:36:57,420 --> 00:37:07,560
you can have peace that transcends all understanding, and that transcends all circumstances.

457
00:37:07,560 --> 00:37:11,800
That's what I can feel.

458
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:13,140
I hear that.

459
00:37:13,140 --> 00:37:16,360
I've been before you today, Andrew.

460
00:37:18,800 --> 00:37:29,940
I don't know where everybody's in here, but a room beside somebody, many of us probably desperately needed.

461
00:37:29,940 --> 00:37:45,320
And my prayer this morning that your spirit would come over and that peace like a river with that 10-hour wind would fall over us this morning,

462
00:37:45,320 --> 00:37:48,380
that we would know that you love us and that we're safe in you.

463
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:54,720
And that the peace that transcends all understanding and all circumstances would come to pass.

464
00:37:54,720 --> 00:37:57,340
In the name of your Son, Jesus, we pray.

465
00:37:57,340 --> 00:37:58,040
Amen.
